{
    "65854": {
        "order_id": 1,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "algebra",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) Given that (7 -2x), 9, (5x + 17) are consecutive terms of a Geometric Progression (G. P) with common ratio, r&gt;0, find the values of x.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Two positive numbers are in the ratio 3:4. The sum of thrice the first number and twice the second is 68. Find the smaller number.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>&nbsp;(a) r =\\(\\frac{9}{7-2x}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{5x+1}{7-2x}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{9}{7-2x}\\)&nbsp;= \\(\\frac{5x+1}{7-2x}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>9x9=(7-2x) (5x +17)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;81 = 35x + 119 - 10x\\(^2\\) - 34x</p>\r\n\r\n<p>10x\\(^2\\) - x - 38</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(x -2)(10x+19) = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = 2,&nbsp; x = \\(\\frac{19}{10}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Let the integers be x and y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x:y= 3:4</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{x}{y}\\) =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = \\(\\frac{3y}{4}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3x&nbsp;+ 2y=68</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3(&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)y)+ 2y = 68</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;\\(\\frac{9}{4}\\)y + 2y = 68</p>\r\n\r\n<p>9y + 8y = 272</p>\r\n\r\n<p>17y = 272</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y= 16</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) * 16&nbsp;&rarr;12</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65855": {
        "order_id": 2,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "calculus",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>Given that y =(\\(\\frac{pr}{m} - p^2r\\))\\(^{\\frac{-3}{2}}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) make r the subject;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) find the value of r when y = -8, m = 1 and p = 3.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a)&nbsp;y =(\\(\\frac{pr}{m} - p^2r\\))\\(^{\\frac{-3}{2}}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y = (\\(\\frac{pr - mrp^2}{m})^\\frac{-3}{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y = [\\(\\frac{m}{pr - mrp^2}]^\\frac{3}{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(y^\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{m}{r(p - mp^2)}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{m}{y^\\frac{2}{3}[p - mp^2]}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>b) Given y = -8, m = 1 p = 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{m}{y^\\frac{2}{3}[p - mp^2]}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{1}{(-8)^\\frac{2}{3}[ 3&nbsp;- (1)3^2]}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{1}{(-2)^2[3&nbsp;- 9]}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>r = \\(\\frac{1}{[4][-6]}\\) = \\(\\frac{-1}{24}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 1,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65856": {
        "order_id": 3,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "lengths-and-perimeters",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>A chord subtends an angle of 72&ordm;&nbsp;at the centre of a circle of radius 24.5m. Calculate the perimeter of the minor segment. [Take &pi; = \\(\\frac{22}{7}\\)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": "https://myschool.ng/storage/classroom/ViO7UCiUKdDPmgeLMTPu61x2wyOIwFu4H1q5Hisj.jpeg",
        "explanation": "<p>From &Delta;OKB</p>\r\n\r\n<p>sin 36&deg; =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{|KB|}{24.5}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>|KB| =&nbsp;0.5878 x 24.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;=14.4011m</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Or</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Length of arc = \\(\\frac{72}{360} * 2 *{\\frac{22}{7}}&nbsp;* 24.7\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=30.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Perimeter = 2(14.4011) + 30.8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 59.6022</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 59.6m</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 10,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 2,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65857": {
        "order_id": 4,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "triangles-and-polygons",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>In the diagram, BCDE is a circle with centre</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A. <strong>&ang;</strong>BCD = (2x + 40)&deg;, <strong>&ang;</strong>BAD = (5x - 35)&ordm;, <strong>&ang;</strong>BED = (2y+ 10)&deg; and <strong>&ang;</strong>ADC=40&quot;. Find:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) the values of x and y;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": "nigeria/exam_image/question_image/WAEC/Mathematics/year/Theory/2022/img_65857.jpeg",
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) 2x + 40 + 2y + 10 = 180&deg;...(1)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2x + 2y = 130</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x + y = 65&ordm;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5x - 35 = 2(2y+ 10) ... (2)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5x - 35 = 4y +20</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5x - 4y = 55</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5x - 4(5-x) = 55</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5x - 260 + 4x =55</p>\r\n\r\n<p>9x = 315</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;x = 35&deg;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y= 65 - 35</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y=30&deg;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ang;ABC + [2 x &ordm;35 + 40] + [5(35)-350)] + 40&deg; =360&ordm;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ang;ABC + 110 + 140&deg;+ 40&ordm; = 360</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ang;ABC + 290&deg; = 360&deg;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ang;ABC = 70&deg;</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 8,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 3,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65858": {
        "order_id": 5,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "probability",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>a) Given that m = tan 30&ordm; and n = tan 45&ordm;, simplify, without using calculator, \\(\\frac{ m - n}{mn}\\), leaving the answer in the form p + \\(\\sqrt{q}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>b) There are 20 women in a&nbsp;bus. 15 of them wear glasses and 10 wear wristwatches. If a woman is chosen at random from the bus, find the probability&nbsp;that she wears both glasses and wristwatches.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": "https://myschool.ng/storage/classroom/xyReGw7MYOtr2PpjYMikyhu9W3MRGi4jiZqLEhnI.png",
        "explanation": "<p>a) m = tan 30&ordm; = \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}, n = tan 45&ordm; = 1</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{ m - n}{mn}\\), = \\(\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}&nbsp;- 1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(1)}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=&nbsp; \\(\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=&nbsp;&nbsp; \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\\) X&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) =&nbsp; \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=&nbsp;\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) x&nbsp;&nbsp;\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=&nbsp;&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3 - 3\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) = 1 - \\(\\sqrt{3}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>b) see the diagram above..</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let the number of women wearing both wristwatches and glasses be x</p>\r\n\r\n<p>15 - x + x + 10 - x = 20</p>\r\n\r\n<p>25 - x = 20</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Therefore, the number of women wearing wrist watches only = 10 - x = 10 - 5 = 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and number of women wearing glasses only = 15 - x = 15 - 5 = 10</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Pr(both) = \\(\\frac{5}{20}\\) = \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) = 0.25</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 10,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 4,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65860": {
        "order_id": 6,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "graph-of-linear-and-quadratic-functions",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>The graph shows the relation of the form y = mx\\(^2\\) + nx + r, where m, n and r are constants.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Using the graph:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) state the scale used on both axes; (b) find the values of m, n and r; (c) find the gradient of the line through P and Q; (d) state the range of values of x for which y &gt; Q.</p>",
        "question_image": "nigeria/exam_image/question_image/WAEC/Mathematics/year/Theory/2022/img_65860.jpeg",
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) x-axis: 2 cm to 2 units or 1 cm to 1 unit</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y-axis: 2 cm to 10 units or 1 cm to 5 units</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) x = -2, x = 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(x+2)(x-4) = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x\\(^2\\)&nbsp;-4x + 2x -8 = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x\\(^2\\)&nbsp;-2x - 8 = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y = 8 + 2x - x(curve has a max. point)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>m = -1,n = 2, r =8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) P(-5,-27),Q(3,5)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Gradient = \\(\\frac{5+27}{3+5}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{32}{8}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;(d) Range: {x:-2 &lt; x &lt; 4)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": null
