    "65864": {
        "order_id": 7,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "ratios-proportions-and-rates",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) A man purchased 180 copies of a book at N250.00 each. He sold y copies at N300.00 each and the rest at a discount of 5 kobo in the Naira of the cost price.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If he made a profit of N7,125.00, find the value of y.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) A trader bought x bags of rice at a cost C = 24x + 103 and sold them at a price, S = \\(\\frac{x^2}{20} - 33x\\).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Find the expression for the profit (i) If 20 bags of rice were sold,</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) calculate the percentage profit.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) Total cost 180 x 250</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=N45,000.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Total selling price = 300y + (180-y) x&nbsp;250 x&nbsp;\\(\\frac{95}{100}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>300y + 42750 -237.5y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 62.5y + 42750</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Profit =&nbsp; 62.5y + 42750 -4500</p>\r\n\r\n<p>7125 =&nbsp;62.5y - 2250</p>\r\n\r\n<p>9375 = 62.5y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y = 150</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b)) Profit = \\(\\frac{x^2}{20} - 33x\\) (24x+ 103)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;9x - \\(\\frac{x^2}{20}\\) -&nbsp;103</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) Cost = 24(20) +103 = 583.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Selling Price =33(20) -&nbsp; \\(\\frac{20^2}{20}\\) = 640</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Percentage profit = \\(\\frac{640-583}{583}\\) x 100%</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 9.78%</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 4,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 1,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "65866": {
        "order_id": 8,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "financial-arithmetic",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:100px\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Item</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>food &amp; drinks</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>fuel</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>rent</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>building project</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>education</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>savings</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Percentage%</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>35</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1.0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>15</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>17.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>x</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>The table shows the monthly expenditure (in percentages) of Mr. Okafor&#39;s salary.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) Calculate the percentage of Mr. Okafor&#39;s salary that was&nbsp;put into savings.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Illustrate the information on a pie chart.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) If Mr. Okafor&#39;s annual gross salary is&nbsp;$28,800.00 and he pays tax of 12%.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Calculate; (i) his monthly tax; (ii) the amount saved each month.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) 35 + 7.5 + 10 + 15 + 17.5 + x = 100</p>\r\n\r\n<p>85 + x = 100.<br />\r\nx = 100 - 85</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = 15</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:200px\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>items</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>%</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>degree</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>food &amp; drinks</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>35</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\\(\\frac{35}{100} * 360\\) = 126&ordm;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>fuel</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\frac{7.5}{100} * 360\\) = 27&ordm;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>rent</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>10</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\frac{10}{100} * 360\\) = 36&ordm;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>building project</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>15</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\frac{15}{100} * 360\\) = 54&ordm;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>education</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>17.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\frac{17.5}{100} * 360\\) = 63&ordm;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>savings</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>15</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\frac{15}{100} * 360\\) = 54&ordm;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Open photo\" src=\"https://scontent.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.15752-9/315529353_5436731309786204_1983618396242083770_n.jpg?_nc_cat=104&amp;ccb=1-7&amp;_nc_sid=aee45a&amp;_nc_eui2=AeHWPsmCQdYLhJ0rgSSsLtS-aoqWr6D9CbZqipavoP0Jttv_G_m2r6M4etweHO1lm1GKTqpPFiNTMGleRBKEg5fz&amp;_nc_ohc=XbNWu4rNEkYAX_YHjVt&amp;_nc_ad=z-m&amp;_nc_cid=0&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.xx&amp;oh=03_AdRQchfgUBpHbxjmYXgj7zQtUkZFMTD-d8A9p1jGd8Hp9A&amp;oe=63AC10F9\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) income tax =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{12}{100} * 28,800\\) = $3,456.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Monthly tax =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{3456}{12}\\) = $288.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) Monthly net salary =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{1}{12} &nbsp;(288 - 3456)\\) = $2,112.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Amount saved each month =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{15}{100} * 2112\\) = $316.80</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
