        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) The diameter of a cylinder closed at both ends is 7cm. If the total surface area is 209cm\\(^2\\), calculate the height. [Take pi = 22/7].</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) The points X and Y, 19m apart are on the same side of a tree. The angles of elevation of the top, T, of the tree from X and Y on the horizontal ground with the foot of the tree are 43&ordm; and 38&deg; respectively.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(i) Illustrate the information in a diagram. (ii) Find, correct to one decimal place, the height of the tree.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": "https://myschool.ng/storage/classroom/zpaJcZCymspSleSAJfEu9hPD55QtnqGOoUMXf0wb.jpeg",
        "explanation": "<p>209 = 2 * \\(\\frac{22}{7}\\) *&nbsp;\\((\\frac{7}{2})^2\\) + 2 *&nbsp;\\(\\frac{22}{7}\\) *&nbsp;\\(\\frac{7}{2}\\) * h</p>\r\n\r\n<p>209 = 77 + 22h</p>\r\n\r\n<p>132 = 22h</p>\r\n\r\n<p>h = 6cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) tan 43&ordm; =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{h}{y}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>0.9125y = h ...[i]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>tan 38&ordm; =&nbsp;\\(\\frac{h}{y+19}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>0.7813(y+19) = h ...[ii]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>0.7813(y+19) =&nbsp;0.9125y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>0.7813y + 14.8447 = 0.93257</p>\r\n\r\n<p>14.8447 = 0.1512y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y= 98.1792</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 98.2m</p>\r\n\r\n<p>h = 0.9325 x 98.1792</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 91.55</p>\r\n\r\n<p>=91.6m</p>",
